tacra: rip the identifiers out, as asked on 11 October: a three-field binding, no rrp_id in the configuration

The binding value is SHA-512 over the freshness element, the Target and the subject, each length-prefixed: no field
for a Relying Party identifier, empty or otherwise, and no server identifier (TheBankster/rats-tacra#20; Mark Novak in
TWI-Unified-Model/globalsign-est#4, 11 October 2026: rip it all out, put back only what is needed once the end-to-end
understanding is there). The RRP entries of the configuration carry no rrp_id and the server checks none against the
RRP's attest-initiate answer; the mock's est.BindingDigest computes the same octets. The same change as the transfer
branch's b531556, and the bench's sample configuration (-sampleconfig) without rrp_id.

